  "comment": "Cost OSPF uses a reference bandwidth of 100 Mbps (10^8) for cost calculation. The formula to calculate the cost is reference bandwidth divided by interface bandwidth ; Interface Cost= 10^8/(interface bandwidth). Calculated values are rounded up to the nearest single decimal value. This means that OSPF will calculate interfaces with speeds higher than 10 Mbps as a cost of 1 (Table 1). T he result",
